OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Tue 17 Nov to Thu 26 NovFA
OL,6,Fgradual transition to more changeable
OL,7,Fconditions is expected at the start of
OL,8,Fthe period. This will allow areas of
OL,9,Flow pressure to move in from the
OL,10,FAtlantic and bring occasional bands of
OL,11,Frain and periods of windy weather,
OL,12,Fhowever these look to be more focussed
OL,13,Facross southern areas, at least
OL,14,Finitially. Whereas northern areas are
OL,15,Flikely to remain in the colder, but
OL,16,Fgenerally drier and brighter
OL,17,Fconditions, for a little longer.
OL,18,FOverall, this period is likely to be
OL,19,Fwetter than average for the majority
OL,20,Fof the country. And whilst colder
OL,21,Fconditions will be possible at times,
OL,22,Fit will often be mild, with
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Ftemperatures near or a little above
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Faverage for the time of year,
OL,25,Fparticularly in the south.
